+Two-dimensional row packing on the retained persistent path (this round's
+mechanism): the persistent body already gives one program per (batch, shared KV
+head) with 32 programs, single-block K/V and one handoff chain per tile, so what
+is left inside a tile is the Q load and the output store pattern.  The actual
+TTIR shows both as single 128x128 block transfers with a row multiplier of 8192
+elements and unit column stride, i.e. 128 segments of 256B at 16KB row distance
+per tile, and the simulator windows of case4 put the largest non-wait cost on
+those copies (veccore MTE3 UB->OUT B16, 16 calls, 37.11/37.15us, plus a second
+15.58/14.96us group; Cube idle 66.3%, VEC idle 59.8%).  Because the G query
+heads sharing one KV head are adjacent in BSND and their 128 channels are
+contiguous, one tile can instead cover SL = BLOCK_M/G sequence positions times
+those G heads and the Q tile becomes a pure 2D [SL, G*128] block whose rows are
+G*128 consecutive elements: the tile's segment count drops from BLOCK_M to SL
+(8x fewer for case4/case7) at unchanged bytes.  An ordered (row-major) reshape
+to [BLOCK_M, BLOCK_D] feeds the unchanged QK / fp32 softmax / single fp16 PV, and
+the output takes the inverse reshape and the same 2D store layout.  Row r of the
+reshaped tile is (sequence sl = r // G, head gi = r % G), so every output row is
+the same (b, s, hq, :) row as before and accumulates the same KV products in the
+same order; only the tile's row order and thus the DMA segmentation changes.
+This is a distinct lowering from the failed 3D [SL, G, D] attempt: no 3D tensor,
+no join/transpose and no scratch buffer -- one 2D load, one reshape in, one
+reshape out.  The predicate is metadata-only (persistent path, actual D == 128,
+G a power of two dividing 128, S divisible by SL and by BLOCK_M, and sd == 1 /
+sh == BLOCK_D for Q and Out), so the causal case1, the G=12 case2 and the
+generic fallback keep their code paths verbatim.  Risks kept open: the reshape
+may lower to a real layout conversion (an extra UB tile, near the 196608B
+budget) or be rejected by the backend; the official four-case checker and the
+post-change IR decide.
